### Import Hooks {% raw %}{#import-hooks}{% endraw %}
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

The `preprocs=` argument names the **import hooks** the body is filtered through as it is staged: the default `mk.compile` compiles any body, `stream.echo` passes it through verbatim, and a colon-delimited list chains several left to right.

{% set pipe_mk %}
# default -- compile cmk-lang (safe for any body)
$(call import.module, def=MyModule)

# verbatim -- body needs no compilation
$(call import.module, def=MyModule preprocs=stream.echo)

# two stages, left to right
$(call import.module, file=lib.mk preprocs=stream.echo:mk.compile)
{% endset %}
{% set pipe_cmk %}
# default -- compile cmk-lang (safe for any body)
cmk.import.module(def=MyModule)

# verbatim -- body needs no compilation
cmk.import.module(def=MyModule preprocs=stream.echo)

# two stages, left to right
cmk.import.module(file=lib.mk preprocs=stream.echo:mk.compile)
{% endset %}
{{site.inline_mirror('mirror_pipelines', pipe_mk, pipe_cmk, default='cmk')}}

The hooks only ever read the source; the original `define`/file is left exactly as written.
